<title>JAPAN: Japan MOF says will watch yen moves 'for a while'.</title>
<headline>Japan MOF says will watch yen moves 'for a while'.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan will watch the yen's moves &quot;for a while&quot;, Finance Minister Hiroshi Mitsuzuka said on Monday.  </p>
<p>Asked about the yen's rise this morning, Mitsuzuka told reporters: &quot;We will watch it for a while.&quot;</p>
<p>The dollar fell below 113 yen in early Tokyo on Monday, its lowest level since May 21.</p>
<p>The U.S. currency closed at 114.33/43 yen on Friday in New York.</p>
</text>
